Native FreeBSD KMS (kernel mode-setting) driver framework.

Written from scratch, no LinuxKPI shim.  Provides drm_device /
drm_file / drm_gem / drm_prime / drm_atomic / drm_mode_* plumbing and
the DRM ioctl surface (44 ioctls implemented, poll(2) and EVFILT_READ
on /dev/dri/cardN, per-plane atomic_check hook, per-plane format
modifiers).  Xorg's modesetting driver and simple Wayland compositors
work against it once a hardware driver attaches to a real display
engine.

This port installs only the framework (kms.ko).  Vendor drivers live
in sys/dev/kms/drivers/ in the source tree and have their own build
requirements (rk_kms needs the out-of-tree FUSB302 USB-C PD driver;
igen targets Intel Gen9+ on amd64).  Build them separately from the
source drop after installing this port.

Source repository: https://github.com/b1nc0d3x/kms-driver
